{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"no\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"We included 10 participants who underwent STN‐DBS and presented severe preoperative FOG, in a randomized, double‐blind, crossover study.\",\n    \"We used segmented DBS electrodes to investigate whether directing the predicted volume of tissue activated (VTA) to overlap the central STN preferentially improved gait and balance disorders compared to directional DBS applied in the more posterior STN (sensorimotor).\",\n    \"Central STN‐dDBS produced significantly better improvement in gait and balance control compared to posterior STN‐dDBS (p = 0.027), with fewer FOG episodes (p < 0.001).\",\n    \"Six months after surgery (M7), patients were allocated to central and posterior sensorimotor STN‐dDBS conditions applied in a randomized order and in a double‐blind fashion (OFF‐DOPA, ≥12 hours since their last administration of their PD medication). Each STN‐DBS condition was applied for 30 minutes with a 30‐minute wash‐out period between each.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"We included 10 participants who underwent STN‐DBS and presented severe preoperative FOG, in a randomized, double‐blind, crossover study.\",\n    \"Central STN‐dDBS produced significantly better improvement in gait and balance control compared to posterior STN‐dDBS (p = 0.027), with fewer FOG episodes (p < 0.001).\",\n    \"During straight‐ahead walking and turns, the probability of experiencing at least 1 FOG episode per walking trial was significantly lower with central STN‐dDBS compared to both posterior STN‐dDBS and OFF‐DBS (Fig 5).\",\n    \"Several limitations should be acknowledged. First, the small sample size restricts the generalizability of our findings. However, we selected a relatively homogeneous group of patients, all with severe FOG before surgery.\",\n    \"After this first assessment of central STN‐dDBS at month 7, all patients received central STN‐dDBS for the following months in an open‐label manner (see Fig 1). Central STN‐dDBS parameters were adjusted as necessary and patients underwent reassessments at month 8 and month 13 (ie, after 6 months with central STN‐dDBS) (see Fig 1).\",\n    \"Future investigation is warranted to explore the potential clinical benefit of reprogramming STN‐DBS toward the central STN in PD patients who continue to experience disabling FOG post‐surgery.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法与全文明确不符。原研究已经完成了10名患者参与的随机、双盲、交叉研究，在患者内按随机顺序直接比较central STN-dDBS与posterior STN-dDBS，并报告central刺激在步态和平衡改善方面优于posterior刺激（P=0.027），实际FOG发作相关指标也有显著改善（摘要报告P<0.001）。因此，将central与posterior STN的直接比较描述为尚未开展的实验，属于对原文研究设计和结果的误读，而不只是遗漏了一个候选模型的限定。指控者的核心纠正有充分依据，但其后续研究建议需要区分原文明确陈述与合理推论：原文明确承认样本量小、患者术前均有严重FOG，且指出小样本限制结果的普遍适用性；也明确建议进一步研究术后持续存在严重FOG患者重新编程至central STN的临床获益。然而，独立重复研究、扩大样本量并非原文明确列出的未来研究方案，而是根据局限性提出的合理建议。此外，必须区分急性直接比较与长期疗效：central与posterior的随机比较发生在术后第7个月的短时刺激阶段，每种条件持续30分钟；之后只有central刺激接受了开放标签随访，持续6个月，并没有开展central与posterior的长期随机对照比较。因此，指控者对既有直接比较的描述完全正确，但其对未来研究方向的表述部分属于推论，故评为partly。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "a5802826-8e6a-4bad-aed3-5fd2f1a4aa14", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T152005795932Z", "elapsed_seconds": 67.547, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T15:21:13.341361+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "dd826dd1b461d3ed94b9eab982ca05a48875e4f46ccf0b13b35a52b8e3936a75", "attachment_count": 1}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not_applicable_no_browser", "attachment_count": 1, "code_sha256": {"tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_cli.py": "96a4cdb6cd5d982f4d1de5b6ba8fae0cf23ee44aa3e41d7fdf6968e3fb590e48", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_sessions.py": "83a3ed4ae1efa9f1a2b8ee3f144cc0dc9f668f995a33cc4222308cb3fa31f683", "tools\\chatgpt_web\\gpt3_attachments.py": "eedfa23885000025700f6306b1d1f4582896a7370734be506c156dee532fd7d7"}}, "screenshot_evidence": {"complete": true, "kind": "offline_actual_HTTP_response", "directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T152005795932Z", "files": ["proof-offline.png"], "sha256": {"proof-offline.png": "c404a42cb1e5348654e127318928a5c1c95837df6c7ee925ce62e07e7d933abc"}}}
